#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:1
msgid "Batch mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:3
msgid ""
"`--batch` / `-b` takes a CSV, **one job per row**. It is the way to "
"describe many extractions once and run them as a unit, and it is also "
"where the highest-precedence configuration source lives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:6
msgid "The batch columns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:7
msgid ""
"Recognised case-insensitively, with spaces and underscores equivalent — "
"`save pdf`, `Save_PDF` and `SAVE PDF` are one column."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md
msgid "Column"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md
msgid "Sets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md
msgid "`url`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md
msgid "the report's URL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md
msgid "`pdf`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md
msgid "one or more document specifiers, pipe-separated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md
msgid "`format`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md
msgid "the format for this row"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md
msgid "`save pdf`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md
msgid "whether to keep a downloaded PDF: `true` or `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md
msgid "`target list`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md
msgid "the target lists for this row, taken **whole**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:25
msgid ""
"An **unrecognised column is an error**, not something ignored. A "
"misspelled column that is silently dropped configures nothing and says "
"nothing about it, and the user is left believing a setting took effect — "
"the same principle as the configuration file's unknown keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:29
msgid "A header with no data rows produces **no jobs**, which is not an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:31
msgid "How `url` and `pdf` combine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:33
msgid ""
"The `pdf` cell is always split on the pipe, even when it holds a single "
"element, and what happens next depends on how many elements come out:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:36
msgid ""
"**one element** is treated as the *singular* specifier, and a `url` in "
"the same row overrides its URL field. The two can therefore never "
"conflict — a common row is a URL in one column and a destination path in "
"the other;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:39
msgid ""
"**several elements** are a genuine plural, and a `url` alongside them "
"**is a conflict**, exactly as in the other configuration sources: one of "
"the two would have to win silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:42
msgid ""
"Rows are numbered from one, the header not counting, and every error "
"names its row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:44
msgid "Precedence: the row wins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:46
msgid ""
"A batch row has the **highest precedence of any configuration source** — "
"above the command line, above the environment, above the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:49
msgid ""
"That inversion is deliberate. In batch mode the command line describes "
"the *run* and the row describes *this job*, and the more specific "
"statement should be the one that holds. It is what lets a single "
"invocation set the output path, the repository and the parallelism once, "
"while each row says only what makes it different."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:58
msgid "One run, still one set of tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:60
msgid ""
"Batch mode does not change what is produced. Every job's results "
"accumulate and are written once, at the end, by the parent process — a "
"batch of ten reports gives one `investments.csv` with a `Report` column, "
"not ten directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/user/advanced/batch.md:64
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"This is also why job-level parallelism uses child processes that **send "
"their results back** rather than each writing its own output: writing per"
" child would have changed the meaning of batch mode. See "
"{doc}`parallelism` and {doc}`../../../reference/design/parallelism`."
msgstr ""

